2026-06-29 14:11:27,587 | INFO | HTTP Request: POST http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
2026-06-29 14:11:27,587 | AGENT | SecurityCompliance Agent answered: As SecurityCompliance Agent at Faber IA, I can confirm that our company has implemented various security controls and measures to ensure compliance with the GDPR and other applicable frameworks. 

We have obtained ISO 27001 certification since 2023, which covers the development, delivery, and operations of our services, including the protection of personal and health data. Additionally, we hold ISO 27701 certification, which is an extension for privacy information management.

To address the client's demands, we will implement the following security controls and measures: 

We use encryption in transit with TLS 1.3 and encryption at rest with AES-256. Our key management is based on EU-based infrastructure. We also apply pseudonymisation and data minimization principles, and our clients can configure data retention according to their needs.

Our platform ensures strict isolation between client corpora, with per-engagement logical separation, and we have implemented role-based access control (RBAC) and audit logging of access and system outputs. 

We have appointed a Data Protection Officer (DPO), maintain a data processing register, and have a Data Processing Agreement (DPA) available that aligns with GDPR Article 28.

For explainability and auditability, our product Atelier provides grounded-in-sources information, retrieval trace, and audit log, supporting a posteriori review and medical confidentiality. 

We also follow secure software development life cycle practices, including code review, dependency scanning, secrets management, and periodic penetration testing by an external CREST-equivalent provider.

Regarding decision automation, we will ensure that our AI solution operates as a non-decisional support tool, providing explainable recommendations or suggestions that require explicit validation by authorized professionals before any decision is made. 

These measures demonstrate our commitment to ensuring the security and compliance of our services with the GDPR, EU AI Act, and other applicable frameworks, addressing the client's demands for strict GDPR compliance, personal and health data protection, medical confidentiality, explainability, and auditability.
